Airflow Core Components
Metadata DB: Information about data such as DAG execution details, task details etc. All historical and logs are stored. 
DAG Processor: It will scan,parse and read entire dags in dag folder and store all information into Metadata DB. 
API Server: It is a middleman to perform communication between all components in Airflow architecture. 
Schedular: Schedule duration of execution of entire DAG. 
Executor: It will generate worker to execute task. 
Worker: Worker are real executors that executes task
Queue: It priotize execution of task
Triggerer: When any complex task takes time to execute worker will give this task to triggerer and it will take next task based on priority and when that complex task completely executed then triggerer will notify to worker

Airflow Architecture
When Developer create DAG
DAG processor parsed entire DAG inside DAG folder 
store all information by converting it into serialized JSON format DAG in Metadata DB
API server help to communicate between each component in this architecture
Schedular reads entire DAG information from Metadata DB and create pre-queue for all task
and provide this queue to executor
Executor will priotize each task in main queue and tells worker to execute each task based on priority
when any task delayed in execution because of complex logic or any reason worker will handover that task to
triggerer and it will move to next task execution based on priority. 
when that task will completely execute then triggerer will notify to worker then worker
will store that task to MetadataDB again schedular read data from it and perform same process. 

What is DAG, Task, Operators
DAG: Directed Acyclic Graph it is a workflow contain one or multiple task which are directed in forward direction only and never revert back with nodes and edges just like graph presentation. 
Task: An isolated environment where execution of only one step with an entire workflow. 
Operators: Inside DAG it is a category of each task means task can be python, pyspark, bash etc. 

XCOMs in Airflow
In DAG, o/p of one task is an I/p of another task. Which creates dependency of one task on another task. 

Parallel Tasks 
Simultaneously execution of multiple task at same time. 

Conditional Branches
It is a conditional statement based on specific condition any one of the task executes. 

